# Trivy vulnerability ignore list. `trivy image` auto-loads a `.trivyignore` from its
# current working directory (unless --ignorefile is set). The release scripts
# (hack/common.sh:trivy_scan, invoked by hack/release.sh) run trivy from the repo root,
# so this root-level file is the one picked up. One CVE ID per line; `#` lines are comments.

# CVE-2026-53572 — github.com/kedacore/keda/v2: PostgreSQL scaler connection-string
# parameter injection via incomplete whitespace escaping. Fixed in KEDA 2.20.0.
#
# NOT REACHABLE in this project: eviction-autoscaler imports only
#   github.com/kedacore/keda/v2/apis/keda/v1alpha1   (the ScaledObject API types),
# and never github.com/kedacore/keda/v2/pkg/scalers, where the vulnerable Postgres
# scaler lives. That code is therefore not compiled into the binary. Trivy flags it
# by module version from the Go buildinfo, so this is a reachability false positive.
#
# Removing this suppression requires bumping keda to >= 2.20.0, which cascades to
# k8s.io 0.36, sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime (~0.25, for client-go's HasSyncedChecker
# interface change), and the Go 1.26 toolchain — a multi-dependency upgrade tracked separately.
# Revisit and delete this entry when that upgrade lands.
CVE-2026-53572
